===Verb===

{{en-verb|head=[[stay]] [[behind]]|stays behind|staying behind|stayed behind}}
# {{&lit|stay|behind}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Effective Cycling| edition=6| page=393| books.google.com/books?isbn=0262560704| author=John Forester| year=1993| passage=If you can, sprint ahead and stay ahead — otherwise slow down and '''stay''' well '''behind'''}}
#* '''1995''', Rudolf Steiner, Helen Fox (original translator), revising translator not named, ''Lecture 7'', ''The Kingdom of Childhood'', Revised Translation, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=181yvCb9-x4C&pg=PA120&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school&hl=en&sa=X&ei=UylAUd6zF8fEkQW_xIDYCw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school&f=false page 120],
#*: Children who are in any way below standard come into this class from all the other classes.
#*: Otherwise, as I have said, we do not let the children '''stay behind''' but we try to bring them along with us under all circumstances, so that in this way each child really receives what is right for his or her particular age.
#* '''1997''', Helen Horne, Sally A. Brown, ''500 Tips for School Improvement'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XEszifI7UwUC&pg=PA74&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0S5AUYy0K8y-kQWGu4CQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&f=false page 74],
#*: Teamwork is important throughout any school organisation. When people work in isolation, they tend to '''stay behind''' a closed door, locked in with their pupils.
# {{rfd-sense}} {{idiomatic}} To [[remain]] where one is, whilst others [[leave]].
#* '''2005''', Al Kelly, ''Challenging Modern Physics: Questioning Einstein's Relativity Theories'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XVLmihZnsvUC&pg=PA24&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=-BhAUfGVLoWPkAXmo4HICA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22&f=false page 24],
#*: If a twin goes off on a spaceship for a long trip at nearly the speed of light, that twin would be much younger on return to earth than the twin who '''stayed behind''' (Fock, 1964; French, 1968; Hawking, 1988; Young, 1992).
#* '''2007''', David W. P. Elliott, ''The Vietnamese War: Revolution and Social Change in the Mekong Delta, 1930-1975'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=JcUpuSZ5Cg8C&pg=PA91&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=-BhAUfGVLoWPkAXmo4HICA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22&f=false page 91],
#*: Much as Tra wanted to '''stay behind''', as commander of the region, it was his duty to organize and lead the troops going to the North.
#* '''2009''', A. Dirk Moses, ''Empire, Colony, Genocide: Conquest, Occupation, and Subaltern Resistance in World History'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=q5C3Sbe1iMoC&pg=PA114&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=-BhAUfGVLoWPkAXmo4HICA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22&f=false page 114],
#*: Ross's fortunes differed sharply from those of the principal Choctaw chief, Greenwood LeFlore, who, unlike Ross, signed a removal treaty on behalf of his people, only to '''stay behind''' himself, accept US citizenship, and go on to a distinguished career in Mississippi politics.
# To remain in a classroom or school at the end of teaching, especially to receive punishment.
#* '''1964''', [[w:Paul Keres|Paul Keres]], [[w:Alexander Kotov|Alexander Kotov]], [[w:Harry Golombek|Harry Golombek]] (translator), ''The Art of the Middle Game'', 1989, Dover, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=2kOO3Hv8zLsC&pg=PA32&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0S5AUYy0K8y-kQWGu4CQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&f=false page 32],
#*: When I '''stayed behind''' at school with my school friends after lessons, and managed to play up to a hundred games in a single afternoon, the strategy was simple enough: I castled on the opposite side in the middle of violent (and mutual) King attacks.
#* '''1996''', Louis Cohen, Lawrence Manion, Keith Morrison, ''A Guide to Teaching Practice'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XocEd8Zi5GAC&pg=PA51&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0S5AUYy0K8y-kQWGu4CQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&f=false page 51],
#*: Observe what sanctions the teacher employs with her class in order to enforce the rules. Are individuals kept in after school, for instance, or are they asked to '''stay behind''' at the end of a lesson, or reprimanded in front of the other children?
#* '''2004''', Rebecca Mahon, ''Excel HSC English Study Guide: Billy Elliot'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=ksGcdJNKb-wC&pg=PA110&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0S5AUYy0K8y-kQWGu4CQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&f=false page 110],
#*: One day I had to '''stay behind''' after my boxing class, and I'd just been told that I was a ‘disgrace to the traditions of the boxing hall’.

